# ABP Application Startup

## Module Class
Every ABP package must have a module class:

```csharp
[DependsOn(
    typeof(AbpEmailingModule),
    typeof(AbpCachingModule)
)]
public class MyModule : AbpModule
{
    public override void ConfigureServices(ServiceConfigurationContext context)
    {
        // Configure services
    }

    public override void OnApplicationInitialization(ApplicationInitializationContext context)
    {
        // Application startup logic
    }
}
```

## ASP.NET Core Integration
```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
builder.Host.UseAutofac();
await builder.AddApplicationAsync<MyWebModule>();

var app = builder.Build();
await app.InitializeApplicationAsync();
await app.RunAsync();
```

## Console Application
```csharp
using var application = await AbpApplicationFactory.CreateAsync<MyModule>(options =>
{
    options.UseAutofac();
});
await application.InitializeAsync();
// Use application.ServiceProvider to resolve services
await application.ShutdownAsync();
```

## Application Name
Set via `appsettings.json` or options:
```json
{
  "ApplicationName": "MyApp"
}
```

## Environment
Access via `IAbpHostEnvironment`:
- `IsDevelopment()`, `IsStaging()`, `IsProduction()`
